**(a) YES - 13 of 4096, and they are exactly Table 6-6.**  
Domain is the code's producer: `v = idata & 0xfff00000`, `f = v >> 20`, so `f ? {0.4095}` for every guest word. `(f & (f+1)) == 0` iff `f+1` is a power of two in `1.4096`:

`f = 0,1,3,7,0xf,0x1f,0x3f,0x7f,0xff,0x1ff,0x3ff,0x7ff,0xfff` (13 values).

Table 6-6 (:9586-9598) is those same 13 bit-strings. Header `IOC_W_MASK_1M`.`_4G` is the same 13 immediates. Non-members fail the test (walked, not guessed): `2&3=2`, `5&6=4` (the probe's `0x500000`), `6&7=6`, `0xaaa&0xaab?0`, `4094&4095=4094`. No 14th; no Table 6-6 encoding excluded. Table 6-17 (:10610-10621) is W_MASK `<31:20>` plus RES type X on both sides, so dropping everything except `0xfff00000` is the field, not a second invention.

**(b) NO change to what `lca_pci_conf` reads.** It does `type1 = d->ioc_conf & 1` (`dev_lca.c:195`). For every `idata`, `(idata & 0x3) & 1 == idata & 1`. Bit 1 is stored and never consumed. Nothing else in `GXEMUL-SEC/src` reads `ioc_conf`.

**(c) YES, bit 33 is set.** `IOC_W_BASE_WEN = 0x200000000` (`1<<33`). `0x240000000 & 0x200000000 = 0x200000000`. Residual `0x40000000` is `W_BASE<30>`. SG is clear. `wbase1 wen` / `wen once` therefore do write WEN. Confirmed in `FIX518_detector_run1.out:20` (announce on `0x240000000`) and `:45-48`.

**(d) YES for `+0x1e0` as a hole; the window is bigger than the brief's story.**  
`DEVINIT` maps `LCA_IOC_BASE`, length `0x20000000` (`dev_lca.c:529-531`). `relative_addr = 0x1e0` is inside. `alpha_lcareg.h` has no `+0x1e0`. HRM "accessed at address" list (10200-10646) ends IOC-space at T_BASE1 `1800001A0`; IACK_SC lives at `1A0000000` (outside this mapping). Switch cases I grepped: no `STAT0`/`STAT1`/`SFT_RST`/`PAR_DIS`. So `+0x1e0` does hit `default:`.  
**The same `default:` also swallows documented registers the brief never named:** STAT0 `+0x040`, STAT1 `+0x060`, SFT_RST `+0x0C0` (`:10461`), PAR_DIS `+0x0E0` (`:10496`). S6.4.14 items 1-2 **require** SROM to write SFT_RST and STAT0. Header defines STAT0/STAT1 with full field masks and no SFT_RST. TB_TAG0.7 at `188000000` (`:10697`) are also inside the `0x20000000` window.

