**Not named at W_MASK:** member 6 again - store bits 31:20 even when Table 6-6 says "unsupported", because **nothing consumes the mask** (S5: translation not modelled). "Unsupported" in the HRM is not "keep previous". The detector *commits* to decline-not-store (`wmask0 declined`); that is a design choice, not a hardware obligation. Silent accept of all 12-bit fields (member 4 on the field, no 13-encoding gate) was also unnamed.

`+0x1e0` itself is a real hole; member 3 is the right member **there**. The defect is treating STAT0/SFT_RST as the same hole.

