| `wbase1 live` | `0x240000000` | M11 / M12 | no (M23 is BASE0) |
| `wmask1 live` | `0x3ff00000` | M14 `f==1` | no |
| `wbase0 zero` | `0` | `M_base0_nonzero` (`!= 0` decline) - in 4, **not in 5** | no. (b) at BASE0 **accepts** 0 |
| `wbase1 wen` | `0x240000000` | M11 / M12 | no |

`wbase0 live` is failability-covered as a **side effect of M11/M12**, not of M23. `conf live` and `tbena live` are the two accept rows whose planned (d) mutants leave them green.

