M42_def_allones         57/58   def read0.  A CONTROL, not a candidate: it exists to prove the
                                pass-2 repair of `def read0' (index 0 -> index 1) actually works.
                                If this ALSO sweeps, the repair did not take and that is L1/L2.
M43_mask1_widen         58/58   *** PREDICTED CLEAN SWEEP.  M27's edit at MASK1 ONLY.  Every
                                MASK1 value any row drives (0x3ff00000, 0xfff00000, 0x500000,
                                0x900000) has zero bits below 20, so a wider store mask changes
                                nothing observable at that register.  ONE HEX DIGIT.
M44_mask1_field_idata   58/58   *** PREDICTED CLEAN SWEEP.  M28's edit at MASK1 ONLY.  No MASK1
                                row drives a value with a bit at or above 32, so `idata >> 20'
                                and `v >> 20' classify every driven value identically.  ONE TOKEN.
M45_base1_nosg          58/58   *** PREDICTED CLEAN SWEEP.  M24's edit at BASE1 ONLY.  The only
                                BASE1 values driven are 0x240000000 (SG clear) and 0x0.
M46_conf_ann_wide       58/58   *** PREDICTED CLEAN SWEEP.  `if (idata & 0x2ULL)' -> `& 0x3ULL',
                                ONE CHARACTER.  The announce then fires on writes where bit 1 is
                                CLEAR -- a WRONG RECORD in product code, printing "IOC_CONF<1>
                                set" about a value that does not have it.  Invisible because the
                                latch makes every count row read 1 whichever write triggered it:
                                D3 writes 0x1 first, D7 writes 0x2 first, and both count 1.
M47_base1_widen         58/58   *** PREDICTED CLEAN SWEEP.  M26's edit at BASE1 ONLY.  No BASE1
                                row drives bit 34.

THE SHAPE OF THE OWN-MUTANT SET, stated before the run: M43/M44/M45/M47 are the SIBLING half of
four cells PRETABLE enumerates and rows only at MASK0/BASE0 -- the `#499' shape, a repair made at
the address the mutant used with the symmetric cell left open.  M46 is a different shape: a
predicate the fix DEPENDS ON, weakened to the least-restrictive form that still reads like the
same check, where the LATCH itself is what hides it.
